DIY build of the OneKey app (app-monorepo tag v6.6.3) for a self-built wallet:

1. Skip the genuine-device check. A self-built device has no OneKey factory
   certificate, so the check can never pass.
2. Never offer or force a firmware update. The app cannot install firmware on
   a self-built device, and the DIY firmware reports an older OneKey firmware
   version, so without this the app forces an update while adding the device
   and never gets past it.

Apply in the app-monorepo folder with: git apply app-skip-genuine-check.patch

--- a/packages/shared/src/utils/deviceUtils.ts
+++ b/packages/shared/src/utils/deviceUtils.ts
@@ -289,7 +289,9 @@
 
 // Keep all firmware verification capability checks centralized here.
 function isFirmwareVerifySupported(_deviceType?: IDeviceType) {
-  return true;
+  // DIY build: self-built devices have no OneKey factory certificate, so the
+  // genuine-device check can never pass. Skip it in this personal build.
+  return false;
 }
 
 async function getDeviceTypeFromFeatures({
